 "design_rationale": "Plant is first-order y_ss=ambient+K*u with tau~170s, delay ~20s. Decay test shows tau/ambient unchanged so Kp for stability still works for K=0.5-1.0 (loop gain Kp*K=0.45-0.9). Persistent offset must be supplied by integral/bias, not P. Single bias-integrator u=bias+Kp*e with bias+=Ki*e*dt learns u_hold without knowing K. Init bias at nominal hold 0.33+(target-0.5)/1.1 so nominal episodes start correct and adapt little; degraded episode with e~0.1-0.2 drives bias 0.33->~0.73 at ~0.002-0.004/s, reaching target in ~250s. Wide limits + anti-windup prevent windup during initial large e and prevent exceeding soft limit 0.85 / hard cutoff 0.9. 12s measurement filter suppresses 0.01 rms noise. Ti=Kp/Ki=45s is > filter and < plant tau, stable for both K values.",
